Package: mossyforest
Title: Network Aware Stability Selection with Random Forests
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Timothy", "Shen", , "tzshen@g.ucla.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Christina", "Ramirez", , "cr@ucla.edu", role = "aut")
    )
Description: An interpretable, network aware random forest feature selection
    framework for high dimensional and correlated data. It combines
    module stratified recursive feature elimination, shadow stability selection,
    and 'TreeSHAP' (Tree SHapley Additive exPlanations) importance, with
    modules either provided by the user or derived with 'WGCNA' (weighted gene
    co expression network analysis). The default backend requires a 'Python'
    environment with 'scikit-learn', 'shap', and 'numpy', which can be
    configured with mf_setup(). A pure 'R' backend based on 'ranger' is also
    available.
